          <p>
            Legion's own comparison tables, which list Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard at about $1.38 per serving, make the budget gap clear. If cost per gram is your main concern, a mainstream whey wins easily. If a stevia-only label and Irish grass-fed sourcing matter to you, Whey+ on sale or in a bundle is a reasonable premium.
          </p>

          <p>
            For a lifter taking one shake a day, the difference between Whey+ and a budget whey is roughly $25 to $30 a month at full price. Use our <a href="/how-much-protein-do-i-need/">protein needs guide</a> to work out whether you need one shake or two before deciding how much the premium is worth.
