          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Momentous Whey Protein Isolate</strong> is the pick for drug-tested athletes. It is NSF Certified for Sport, with 20 g of protein per scoop, and costs more per gram than Whey+. If you need a sport certification, Momentous or Thorne beat Legion; if you do not, Legion gives you more protein per scoop for less. See our <a href="/momentous-protein-powder-review/">Momentous review</a>.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard 100% Whey</strong> is the budget benchmark: about 24 g of protein per scoop from a whey blend led by isolate, with Informed Choice certification according to the brand, at a fraction of Legion's cost per gram. It uses artificial sweeteners in most flavors, which is the main reason Legion buyers avoid it. Read our <a href="/optimum-nutrition-protein-powder-review/">Optimum Nutrition review</a> for the full picture.
