        <div id="skip" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Who Should Skip Legion
          </h2>

          <p>
            <strong>Drug-tested athletes.</strong> Labdoor testing and NSF-registered facilities do not equal NSF Certified for Sport or Informed Sport product certification. Choose a product that appears in those databases instead, such as Momentous or Thorne.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Budget buyers.</strong> At about $2.50 per 25 g of protein for Whey+, Legion costs far more than mainstream wheys that deliver as much or more protein per scoop. If you are fine with sucralose, the savings are substantial. Our <a href="/best-whey-protein-powder/">best whey protein powder</a> guide lists the value leaders.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Anyone who dislikes stevia.</strong> Every Legion protein uses stevia or a stevia-derived sweetener. If its aftertaste bothers you, no Legion flavor will fix that. The no-return guarantee makes a trial low-risk, but go in knowing the sweetener system.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Casein buyers chasing a big dose.</strong> With 21 g of protein per scoop on the supplement panel and a high price, Casein+ is an expensive way to get bedtime protein. A mainstream micellar casein delivers more per scoop for less.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>People with medical conditions.</strong> If you have kidney disease, are pregnant, have a milk allergy or take medication, check with your doctor or a registered dietitian before adding concentrated protein. Nothing here is medical advice.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Reading the casein line instead of the protein line</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Casein+ panels list 25 g of micellar casein but 21 g of protein. The ingredient weight is not the protein dose. Always read the Protein row of the supplement-facts panel when comparing powders, especially when a review or ad quotes a rounder, bigger number. The gap here is about 4 g per scoop.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating an NSF-certified facility as a certified product</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Legion says its products are made in NSF-certified facilities. That is a manufacturing audit, not banned-substance testing of the product. Drug-tested athletes need the exact product listed in the NSF Certified for Sport or Informed Sport database, which Legion's proteins are not at the time of writing.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying full price</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Legion runs frequent sales, bundle discounts and subscription pricing on its own site, and retailer prices vary widely. Buying a single tub at full list price can cost a fifth more than a sale or multi-pack. Compare the brand site, Amazon and large retailers before ordering, and stock up only when the discount is real.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming natural sweeteners taste neutral</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Stevia has a distinctive aftertaste that some people notice strongly. If you have disliked stevia-sweetened drinks before, try a small size or a single flavor first rather than a multi-tub bundle, and use the guarantee if it does not work for you. Mixing it into milk or a smoothie often softens the aftertaste.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring cheaper isolates with bigger scoops</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Whey+ is good, but Transparent Labs delivers about 28 g of protein per scoop with a similar clean label and slightly lower cost per 25 g. Compare cost per gram of protein across clean-label isolates before settling on the one with the best marketing or the most familiar name.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

